/-!
# Pointwise Serrin geometry of generated vorticity shells

This module compiles an actual finite source-generated integer-shell path
into its physical Biot--Savart velocity field.  The endpoint field splits
exactly into the seed field, retained as a literal uncovered residual, plus
the chronological fields written by the generated whole-shell receipts.

The analytic layer bounds the squared Fourier velocity majorant, and hence
the pointwise squared physical velocity, by the reciprocal shell-cardinality
sum times the shell-weighted vorticity amplitude.  The Biot--Savart factor
`(2 * Real.pi)⁻²` remains explicit.

No shell coverage, cardinality estimate, amplitude decay, time occupancy,
target endpoint, or trajectory is accepted as a premise.
-/

namespace SaturationMonoid
namespace NavierStokes
namespace ThreeDimensionalVorticityCoefficientGeneratedShellSerrinGeometry

